    "tea": "Numbers twenty-seven. Their names are Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah and Tirzah. Scripture lists every single one. Their father died in the wilderness with no sons. Under the rules as they stood, land moved through sons. So his name and his portion simply vanish. And these five women do not petition quietly. They stood before Moses. And before Eleazar the priest. And before the princes and all the congregation. At the door of the tabernacle. That is the entire leadership of the nation, plus everybody else, and five sisters walk up and make a legal argument. \"Why should the name of our father be done away from among his family, because he hath no son? Give unto us therefore a possession among the brethren of our father.\" And Moses does not rule on it. He does not wing it. He does not send them home. \"And Moses brought their cause before the Lord.\" And the answer comes back. \"The daughters of Zelophehad speak right.\" Speak right. God agreed with them. On the record. And the inheritance law of Israel was rewritten because five women showed up and asked.",
