    "tea": "Luke chapter eight. Three verses that get skipped constantly. Jesus is going through every city and village preaching, and the twelve are with him. Standard. And then Luke adds, \"and certain women, which had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities.\" And he names them. Mary called Magdalene, out of whom went seven devils. Joanna. Susanna. And many others. Stop on Joanna for a second, because Luke drops her job title like it is nothing. \"Joanna the wife of Chuza Herod's steward.\" Herod's steward. That is a household manager inside the royal court. The same court. That is not a small detail. That is a woman with access, money, and an enormous amount to lose by being on this road at all. And then the line. \"Which ministered unto him of their substance.\" Their substance. Their own resources. Luke did not have to write any of that down. Nobody was auditing him. He wanted somebody two thousand years later to know exactly who was paying for it.",
